00:04:00,964 --> 00:04:02,764
once more, you think?

459
00:04:02,764 --> 00:04:04,674
If possible, with an upset expression.

460
00:04:04,674 --> 00:04:05,764
Upset.

461
00:04:05,764 --> 00:04:06,304
Yes.

462
00:04:07,764 --> 00:04:09,224
Why the blushing?

463
00:04:09,224 --> 00:04:11,144
Did you imagine something?

464
00:04:11,594 --> 00:04:13,434
Say it, girl genius.

465
00:04:13,434 --> 00:04:18,154
Let's hear what the genius thought!

466
00:04:19,294 --> 00:04:21,774
It looks like you're both perverts.

467
00:04:22,064 --> 00:04:22,654
Oh, my...

468
00:04:22,654 --> 00:04:23,484
It's not a compliment.

469
00:04:23,744 --> 00:04:26,654
I would say the person with the perverted imagination is the pervert.

470
00:04:27,074 --> 00:04:28,614
You're a perverted girl genius!

471
00:04:28,984 --> 00:04:30,324
Who's a pervert?

472
00:04:30,744 --> 00:04:31,494
Okay...

473
00:04:31,494 --> 00:04:33,704
To be honest, we're at the point where

474
00:04:33,704 --> 00:04:36,464
I could sue you for sexual harassment this minute, but I'll forget it for now.

475
00:04:36,814 --> 00:04:37,504
For now?

476
00:04:37,504 --> 00:04:39,464
So tell me the details.

477
00:04:39,924 --> 00:04:43,384
This banana has something to do with that microwave, right?

478
00:04:43,384 --> 00:04:44,964
It's top-secret!

479
00:04:44,964 --> 00:04:47,804
Future Gadget #8, the Phone Microwave,

480
00:04:47,804 --> 00:04:50,184
is my lab's secret weapon.

481
00:04:52,264 --> 00:04:57,354
But Miss Makise might be able to explain how this weird thing works.

482
00:04:57,354 --> 00:04:58,064
But...

483
00:04:58,064 --> 00:05:01,734
You need to understand, we'll never figure this out on our own.

484
00:05:02,194 --> 00:05:05,744
But this is the Future Gadget Lab's...

485
00:05:09,664 --> 00:05:10,574
You!

486
00:05:10,574 --> 00:05:12,374
Christina, you said?

487
00:05:12,374 --> 00:05:13,704
No, I never said that.

488
00:05:13,704 --> 00:05:15,954
I'll tell you the secrets of the Phone Microwave,

489
00:05:15,954 --> 00:05:17,374
but on two conditions!

490
00:05:18,134 --> 00:05:23,964
One, you must become a Future Gadget Lab member.

491
00:05:24,344 --> 00:05:27,674
You want me to join your lab?

492
00:05:28,594 --> 00:05:33,304
But I'm returning to America in August...

493
00:05:33,304 --> 00:05:34,604
It can be just until then.

494
00:05:35,104 --> 00:05:36,274
And one more.

495
00:05:36,274 --> 00:05:37,184
There's more?

496
00:05:37,184 --> 00:05:41,024
Forget about any sexual harassment I've done.

497
00:05:42,404 --> 00:05:43,364
That's it.

498
00:05:43,364 --> 00:05:44,904
Okarin, you're a small person.

499
00:05:44,904 --> 00:05:47,534
A very small person.

500
00:05:47,534 --> 00:05:50,074
And I love that. Love it!

501
00:05:50,074 --> 00:05:51,164
Shut up!

502
00:05:51,164 --> 00:05:52,204
Well?

503
00:05:52,204 --> 00:05:53,744
I think the conditions are very favorable...

504
00:05:53,954 --> 00:05:55,584
Favorable to you.

505
00:05:55,584 --> 00:05:56,664
Jeez...

506
00:05:56,664 --> 00:05:58,794
You're making my brain put out too much noradrenaline.

507
00:05:59,084 --> 00:06:00,874
What will you do, Christina?

508
00:06:01,214 --> 00:06:02,924
There's no "-tina!"

509
00:06:02,924 --> 00:06:04,794
Sorry, "The Zombie."

510
00:06:05,154 --> 00:06:07,844
Say it right, Hououin Pervert-Kyouma!

511
00:06:07,844 --> 00:06:08,634
What?

512
00:06:08,634 --> 00:06:10,384
Pervert Girl Genius!

513
00:06:11,264 --> 00:06:13,644
Perverts glaring at each other... Win!

514
00:06:13,644 --> 00:06:15,224
Shut up, pervert!

515
00:06:15,224 --> 00:06:16,604
Oh, fine.

516
00:06:16,974 --> 00:06:17,934
All right.

517
00:06:17,934 --> 00:06:18,974
I accept.

518
00:06:18,974 --> 00:06:20,894
So no more "Pervert."

519
00:06:21,274 --> 00:06:23,234
I'll stop calling you one, too.

520
00:06:23,234 --> 00:06:24,194
Very well.

521
00:06:24,564 --> 00:06:28,234
Then from now on, you're Lab Member 004!

522
00:06:28,534 --> 00:06:30,744
Christina!

523
00:06:30,744 --> 00:06:31,994
No "-tina," either!

524
00:06:32,244 --> 00:06:36,084
Juicy Kara-age #1... Wow!

525
00:06:36,084 --> 00:06:37,914
I'm back!

526
00:06:36,084 --> 00:06:37,914
You think it's a teleporter?

527
00:06:37,914 --> 00:06:40,004
It's dangerous to jump to conclusions.

528
00:06:40,004 --> 00:06:41,714
Then what do you think it is?

529
00:06:41,714 --> 00:06:42,794
If nothing else,

530
00:06:42,794 --> 00:06:46,544
it didn't teleport the Juicy Kara-age or the banana bunch.

531
00:06:43,834 --> 00:06:47,214
One, two, three, four...

532
00:06:47,214 --> 00:06:49,004
A guest?

533
00:06:50,634 --> 00:06:52,174
Hello there.

534
00:06:52,174 --> 00:06:53,554
I'm Makise Kurisu.

535
00:06:53,974 --> 00:06:56,264
I'm sorry to just show up, out of the blue.

536
00:06:56,264 --> 00:06:57,814
Shiina Mayuri.

537
00:06:58,014 --> 00:07:00,684
It looks like I'm a lab member now, too.

538
00:07:01,204 --> 00:07:02,354
A lab member?

539
00:07:02,814 --> 00:07:03,604
Yes...

540
00:07:03,604 --> 00:07:06,984
A girl lab member!

541
00:07:06,984 --> 00:07:09,614
Is it that rare?

542
00:07:09,614 --> 00:07:11,574
Yes! Yes! Yes!

543
00:07:11,574 --> 00:07:15,204
You're the first girl lab member after Mayushii!

544
00:07:15,204 --> 00:07:16,034
I see.

545
00:07:16,534 --> 00:07:17,834
Nice to meet you.

546
00:07:18,184 --> 00:07:19,584
Yes, nice to meet you.

547
00:07:19,584 --> 00:07:20,544
What?

548
00:07:20,954 --> 00:07:21,794
What happened?

549
00:07:21,794 --> 00:07:23,584
There was some electrical release.

550
00:07:24,424 --> 00:07:26,424
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

551
00:07:26,424 --> 00:07:28,254
Give me the details.

552
00:07:28,254 --> 00:07:30,554
Um... Well...

553
00:07:30,554 --> 00:07:33,174
Some kind of lightning came from the microwave.

554
00:07:33,174 --> 00:07:34,224
When?

555
00:07:34,224 --> 00:07:36,514
Yesterday, around noon.

556
00:07:36,894 --> 00:07:40,724
You saw the thing about the satellite crash and ran out,

557
00:07:40,724 --> 00:07:43,024
and I connected my phone to it.

558
00:07:46,734 --> 00:07:49,194
Then, when I sent that message,

559
00:07:49,194 --> 00:07:52,694
your phone was hooked up to the Phone Microwave?

560
00:07:53,004 --> 00:07:55,744
The one about Miss Makise being stabbed?

561
00:07:55,744 --> 00:07:57,494
That was a week ago, wasn't it?

562
00:07:57,494 --> 00:08:00,204
No, that was yesterday!

563
00:08:02,154 --> 00:08:03,584
Where is it? Where is it?

564
00:08:03,584 --> 00:08:04,584
Why isn't it here?!

565
00:08:04,964 --> 00:08:07,424
When this happened, what was the microwave doing?

566
00:08:07,424 --> 00:08:09,504
I was doing a systems test...

567
00:08:09,504 --> 00:08:12,004
So I think it was during the reverse spinning testing.

568
00:08:12,424 --> 00:08:14,174
We should try to recreate this.

569
00:08:14,534 --> 00:08:17,594
Mayuri, bring me the Juicy Kara-age #1!

570
00:08:17,594 --> 00:08:18,394
Okay!

571
00:08:18,724 --> 00:08:20,144
You want some, everyone?

572
00:08:20,144 --> 00:08:22,224
I can give each of you one.

573
00:08:22,224 --> 00:08:23,564
Do we need to put something in there?

574
00:08:23,564 --> 00:08:24,734
I want to see

575
00:08:24,734 --> 00:08:27,024
what happens to its contents when it revolves backwards.

576
00:08:28,354 --> 00:08:28,944
Daru.

577
00:08:32,024 --> 00:08:34,574
Assistant, send a message to my phone.

578
00:08:34,944 --> 00:08:37,364
Since when am I your assistant?

579
00:08:37,364 --> 00:08:39,624
And I don't know your address.

580
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:41,414
Useless assistant.

581
00:08:41,784 --> 00:08:43,544
Daru, your phone's fine.

582
00:08:43,544 --> 00:08:44,914
What should the subject be?

583
00:08:44,914 --> 00:08:45,914
Let me see.

584
00:08:46,374 --> 00:08:48,084
"Christina is a pervert."

585
00:08:48,084 --> 00:08:49,794
I told you that's off-limits.

586
00:08:50,174 --> 00:08:54,464
Then we'll split the difference and go with "Okarin is a pervert"...

587
00:08:54,464 --> 00:08:55,014
What?

588
00:08:55,014 --> 00:08:56,674
Hashida-san, good job!

589
00:08:56,674 --> 00:08:58,594
Okay, sending.

590
00:08:59,894 --> 00:09:02,104
Now we wait for the message to arrive at the phone...

591
00:09:02,104 --> 00:09:04,474
I bet it's ready now!

592
00:09:04,974 --> 00:09:05,934
Wait!

593
00:09:18,954 --> 00:09:20,454
Are you okay?

594
00:09:20,454 --> 00:09:21,784
Yeah...

595
00:09:23,454 --> 00:09:24,794
Gotta turn on the fan!

596
00:09:29,624 --> 00:09:30,794
What is this?

597
00:09:31,424 --> 00:09:33,214
The EM waves maybe?

598
00:09:33,214 --> 00:09:35,004
Don't be stupid.

599
00:09:35,004 --> 00:09:39,724
A microwave's EM waves couldn't split a desk so quickly.

600
00:09:39,724 --> 00:09:41,594
They're all black!

601
00:09:41,964 --> 00:09:44,264
And I just bought them, too!

602
00:09:44,264 --> 00:09:46,104
What do we do about the hole in the floor?

603
00:09:46,104 --> 00:09:48,894
If Mr. Braun finds that, we're in serious trouble.

604
00:09:55,024 --> 00:09:55,864
Well?

605
00:09:55,864 --> 00:09:56,284
It's here.

606
00:09:56,944 --> 00:10:00,614
7/24, 17:30.

607
00:10:01,244 --> 00:10:02,914
<i>It went back to the past...</i>

608
00:10:06,624 --> 00:10:07,834
Did you find something?

609
00:10:07,834 --> 00:10:10,164
Yes. It's all coming together!

610
00:10:10,164 --> 00:10:11,334
I can see it...

611
00:10:11,334 --> 00:10:14,084
The one answer this all points to!

612
00:10:14,084 --> 00:10:15,254
Really?

613
00:10:15,924 --> 00:10:18,964
The banana, split off from the bunch, returned to it!

614
00:10:19,384 --> 00:10:21,514
The message traveled five days into the past.

615
00:10:22,014 --> 00:10:24,054
No way. You can't mean...

616
00:10:24,054 --> 00:10:25,144
That's right!

617
00:10:25,554 --> 00:10:27,644
The Phone Microwave is...

618
00:10:32,064 --> 00:10:33,354
...a time machine!

619
00:10:46,284 --> 00:10:49,334
Thirteen messages?

620
00:10:50,204 --> 00:10:51,874
The lightning...

621
00:10:52,674 --> 00:10:54,124
Oh, right.

622
00:10:54,124 --> 00:10:56,674
I dubbed her the "Shining Finger."

623
00:10:56,674 --> 00:10:59,054
But this many?

624
00:10:59,674 --> 00:11:01,174
"Message me now."

625
00:11:01,174 --> 00:11:03,014
"Are you asleep?"

626
00:11:03,014 --> 00:11:05,054
"How long are you going to sleep?"

627
00:11:05,474 --> 00:11:06,764
Daru?

628
00:11:09,684 --> 00:11:12,024
Wanna go for a walk?

629
00:11:13,564 --> 00:11:14,404
What's wrong?

630
00:11:14,404 --> 00:11:16,234
Damage is pretty bad.

631
00:11:16,234 --> 00:11:18,194
I worked all night, with nothing to show for it.

632
00:11:18,774 --> 00:11:20,694
I regret trying.

633
00:11:21,084 --> 00:11:24,074
Why aren't they turning into gel-banas anymore?

634
00:11:26,284 --> 00:11:27,284
Hell if I know.

635
00:11:27,704 --> 00:11:30,084
That was the only time we were able to send a message.

636
00:11:30,584 --> 00:11:33,254
Shouldn't we call Miss Makise back?

637
00:11:33,624 --> 00:11:35,544
You know that's not happening.

638
00:11:35,544 --> 00:11:36,544
No way.

639
00:11:37,544 --> 00:11:39,044
A time machine?

640
00:11:42,054 --> 00:11:44,434
She never came back.

641
00:11:44,434 --> 00:11:46,344
What was that?

642
00:11:47,304 --> 00:11:48,474
What is this?

643
00:11:48,854 --> 00:11:50,814
The LHC.

644
00:11:51,774 --> 00:11:53,524
The Large Hadron Collider,

645
00:11:53,524 --> 00:11:55,854
SERN's particle accelerator.

646
00:11:56,154 --> 00:11:58,234
Makes you feel better, just looking at it...

647
00:12:02,404 --> 00:12:06,824
<i>SERN maintains an exclusive monopoly on time machines.</i>

648
00:12:08,534 --> 00:12:10,704
John Titor...

649
00:12:11,334 --> 00:12:13,704
Oh, the one you were talking about.

650
00:12:13,704 --> 00:12:16,424
@channel can't get enough of the guy.

651
00:12:16,424 --> 00:12:18,134
What is SERN?

652
00:12:18,134 --> 00:12:23,214
Titor was saying that they finish a time machine by 2034!

653
00:12:23,214 --> 00:12:24,804
I have no idea what you're talking about...

654
00:12:24,804 --> 00:12:26,094
Just tell me!

655
00:12:26,094 --> 00:12:27,054
What is SERN?

656
00:12:27,054 --> 00:12:29,014
Calm down.

657
00:12:29,014 --> 00:12:32,814
It's the acronym for the European Organization in Nuclear Research and Particle Physics.

658
00:12:32,814 --> 00:12:34,854
Its HQ is just outside Geneva.

659
00:12:35,234 --> 00:12:38,904
Like the name suggests, its main work is in particle physics.

660
00:12:38,904 --> 00:12:42,614
And it has some of the world's best facilities for it:

661
00:12:42,614 --> 00:12:44,154
The Low Energy Antiproton Ring.

662
00:12:44,154 --> 00:12:46,364
The Proton Synchrotron Booster.

663
00:12:46,364 --> 00:12:48,454
The Large ElectronâPositron Collider...

664
00:12:48,454 --> 00:12:50,164
And the last boss,

665
00:12:50,664 --> 00:12:52,874
the world's biggest particle accelerator,

666
00:12:52,874 --> 00:12:55,664
Large Hadron Collider-tan!

667
00:12:57,464 --> 00:13:04,214
There were rumors that the LHC could generate a mini-black hole.

668
00:13:06,884 --> 00:13:08,304
A black hole...

669
00:13:08,684 --> 00:13:09,304
Daru.

670
00:13:09,304 --> 00:13:10,014
'Sup?

671
00:13:10,764 --> 00:13:14,854
Didn't one proposed time travel method

672
00:13:14,854 --> 00:13:17,564
use a mini-black hole?

673
00:13:18,274 --> 00:13:20,274
Yeah, it did.

674
00:13:20,274 --> 00:13:23,074
But you heard Miss Makise's lecture, right?

675
00:13:23,524 --> 00:13:26,824
She said creating a black hole was impossible.

676
00:13:26,824 --> 00:13:29,574
But if the LHC exists,

677
00:13:29,574 --> 00:13:31,164
then it's possible...

678
00:13:30,454 --> 00:13:31,164
It is!

679
00:13:31,534 --> 00:13:32,414
No, it isn't.

680
00:13:32,874 --> 00:13:34,544
SERN's publicly denied it.

681
00:13:34,544 --> 00:13:38,124
But they say that where there's smoke, there's fire.

682
00:13:38,504 --> 00:13:39,414
It's me.

683
00:13:38,964 --> 00:13:41,924
No Cell Phones

684
00:13:40,294 --> 00:13:41,884
That's right. I know.

685
00:13:42,294 --> 00:13:44,214
El Psy Congroo.

686
00:13:44,764 --> 00:13:47,054
Who, exactly, are you fighting?

687
00:13:47,054 --> 00:13:50,434
There's only one thing for us to do now.

688
00:13:50,434 --> 00:13:52,054
Go see Feyris-tan!

689
00:13:52,054 --> 00:13:52,764
No!

690
00:13:53,304 --> 00:13:55,014
You're a super haker, right?

691
00:13:55,014 --> 00:13:56,814
You should smile knowingly!

692
00:13:56,814 --> 00:13:58,774
It's "hacker," not "haker," okay?

693
00:13:59,144 --> 00:14:00,274
You understand the rest?

694
00:14:00,274 --> 00:14:01,944
Not a bit.

695
00:14:04,024 --> 00:14:05,194
Hack into SERN.

696
00:14:06,904 --> 00:14:07,944
That's it.

697
00:14:08,784 --> 00:14:10,864
Okarin... This is a joke, right?

698
00:14:11,664 --> 00:14:13,374
You need to find out what evil they're up to

699
00:14:13,374 --> 00:14:15,834
and get a hint about the time machine.

700
00:14:16,704 --> 00:14:20,544
Whether we make the Phone Microwave into a real time machine

701
00:14:20,544 --> 00:14:24,634
or let it rest forever in the lab storeroom, is up to your skills.

702
00:14:24,634 --> 00:14:26,464
Don't blame me for the outcome!

703
00:14:26,464 --> 00:14:28,134
Two orders of gyuudon.

704
00:14:28,134 --> 00:14:29,594
800 yen, total.

705
00:14:29,594 --> 00:14:31,384
Okarin!

706
00:14:34,344 --> 00:14:35,854
Slacking off again?

707
00:14:36,224 --> 00:14:39,314
Yeah, the shop's boring.

708
00:14:39,314 --> 00:14:40,684
Nothing to do.

709
00:14:40,684 --> 00:14:42,904
You're more of a bicycle shop now.

710
00:14:43,654 --> 00:14:47,734
Anyway, what are you doing on the second floor?

711
00:14:47,734 --> 00:14:50,114
Future Gadget Lab, right?

712
00:14:50,114 --> 00:14:51,534
Where did you learn that name?

713
00:14:53,484 --> 00:14:54,374
Future Gadget Lab

714
00:14:55,124 --> 00:14:57,874
If you know that much, then fine.

715
00:14:57,874 --> 00:15:00,504
We're fighting against an organization

716
00:15:00,504 --> 00:15:02,664
that rules the world from the shadows.

717
00:15:03,214 --> 00:15:07,464
Just now, we're hacking into that organization.

718
00:15:08,214 --> 00:15:11,974
So, is SERN that organization?

719
00:15:12,274 --> 00:15:13,474
How did you know?

720
00:15:13,474 --> 00:15:14,474
I'm sorry.

721
00:15:14,474 --> 00:15:17,514
Actually, I overheard you guys.

722
00:15:17,934 --> 00:15:19,724
I said I was bored.

723
00:15:19,724 --> 00:15:20,564
So, accidentally...

724
00:15:20,564 --> 00:15:22,394
You were spying on us?

725
00:15:22,894 --> 00:15:24,694
I can hear you.

726
00:15:24,984 --> 00:15:26,734
But don't worry.

727
00:15:26,734 --> 00:15:28,824
I'm good at keeping my mouth shut.

728
00:15:31,284 --> 00:15:32,244
Again?

729
00:15:32,244 --> 00:15:34,494
What? A message that someone died?

730
00:15:34,494 --> 00:15:35,704
Someone died?

731
00:15:35,704 --> 00:15:38,664
N-No... I was just kidding.

732
00:15:38,664 --> 00:15:41,624
This girl's obsessed with some old PC

733
00:15:41,624 --> 00:15:43,754
called an IBN 5100.

734
